# Gestion Annonces Comments And Realtime

- Use threaded comments only. Replies must use `Comment.parent_id`.
- `Comment.content` is required. `parent_id` is optional, but when present it must reference a comment from the same `listing_id`.
- Only authenticated users can comment.
- On closed groups, comment access may be limited to participants and the seller.
- Add anti-spam protections for repeated comment submissions.
- Before publishing a comment, support abusive-content moderation when enabled.
- Use `Perspective API` to detect toxic, insulting, aggressive, or inappropriate comment content.
- Based on moderation score, a comment may be accepted, rejected, masked, or sent to moderation.
- Listing owner and admin must be able to remove inappropriate comments.
- Realtime updates should cover only meaningful events: new comment, new group participant, group progress, group completion, group expiry, and relevant new listings.
- Use Spring Boot WebSocket + STOMP for realtime delivery.
- Do not implement a full chat system; comments replace chat by design.
